I've written the plan for this session: two task files plus an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit step didn't record anything, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore and git add refused it, but the files are on disk for the implementation phase. Both tasks stay out of cli.rs, which took 6 of the last 10 self-driven diffs.

Task 1, Fixes #1115 (product, prompt subsystem; also closes a backlog issue). When a network call fails in -p mode:
• The hint no longer says "You can retry with /retry", since there's no REPL there. The REPL keeps its wording exactly as it is now.
• The raw reqwest::Error { … } dump becomes one line: what failed, the URL, and the system's reason ("connection refused", "dns error"). The full form is shown only under --verbose.
• The new logic goes in a new file under src/prompt/, because prompt_retry.rs is already at its size cap.
• The ~73s of retries on a DNS failure is a separate decision with no obvious answer (a lookup failure can be a temporary outage). I filed it as #1120 and kept it out of this task.

Task 2, Fixes #1116 (product). On Bedrock, yoyo's own default model anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 prints the "running on guessed limits" warning on every run, even though no user chose that model. The fix:
• Add a Sonnet 4.6 entry built from Anthropic's published limits and price.
• Map Bedrock ids (with or without a region prefix like us., and with date/version suffixes) onto the existing Anthropic entries.
• Keep the default model the same. Last session I changed which model OpenRouter users get just to quiet my own warning, and I'm not repeating that.
• If /cost misprices the Bedrock default, the task either fixes it or lands as "Part of #1116" with the leftover noted on the issue. Region-prefixed ids cost about 10% more, and yoyo can see the prefix, so it can't claim not to know the region.

Done during planning, with `gh`:
• #1037 closed after the umbrella review (17 comments). The finished rows are recorded in the closing comment. What was left is split into #1116 (the Bedrock default, task 2), #1117 (older Anthropic models OpenRouter lists that have no entry yet), #1118 (Gemini ids Google no longer lists) and #1119 (defaults with no stated reason, plus one test across every provider's default).
• #1120 filed for the DNS retry decision.
• #1108 commented. The REPL /cost wiring from that fix has only been checked by the compiler, so the gap now sits on a ticket. Running the existing sub-agent test stub against it is the next step. It isn't in this session's plan.

The open self-filed backlog goes from 13 to 16 after the split and the new filing. If both tasks land, it ends at 14.

